>There is a chance that you will gain teleport control from eating a
>tengu (tengus corpses can confer both teleport and tele control,
>though you won't get both from eating a single corpse).

I used to know the chances in 3.0j, but in 3.1.2, it has changed.  Here's
how I think it works now: A tengu can give one of three possible intrinsics -
poison resistance, teleport, and teleport control.  First nethack picks which 
one to try to give you (regardsless of which you already have).  Although
the code is a little strange, I think it means an equal chance of each
(in this case one in 3).

Once it picks which intrinsic it attempts to give you, you have a 
  6/10 chance if it's teleport
  6/12 chance if it's teleport control
  6/15 chance if it's poison resistance

ie: a 20%   (1/5)  chance of gaining teleport
    a 16.6% (1/6)  chance of gaining teleport control
    a 13.3% (2/15) chance of gaining poison resistance

    a 50% chance of getting nothing (more than 50% if you already
      have one of the above)
